(Regression: the `type` property reports every static declared type.)

a number called num is 3.
a float called flt is 3.5.
a text called txt is "hello".
a boolean called flg is true.
a list called lst is [1, 2].
a map called mp is {"k": 1}.
a buffer called buf is "hi".
open a file for reading called handle at "/dev/null".
create a timer called tmr.
a time called now is current time.

Print "{num's type}".
Print "{flt's type}".
Print "{txt's type}".
Print "{flg's type}".
Print "{lst's type}".
Print "{mp's type}".
Print "{buf's type}".
Print "{handle's type}".
Print "{tmr's type}".
Print "{now's type}".
